{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teorth/optimizationproblems/pulls/280","id":5027643094,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQ_aBz88AAAABK6u-1g","html_url":"https://github.com/teorth/optimizationproblems/pull/280","diff_url":"https://github.com/teorth/optimizationproblems/pull/280.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/teorth/optimizationproblems/pull/280.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teorth/optimizationproblems/issues/280","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teorth/optimizationproblems/pulls/280/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teorth/optimizationproblems/pulls/280/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teorth/optimizationproblems/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teorth/optimizationproblems/issues/280/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teorth/optimizationproblems/statuses/0555894b9eddf5e7685af6cceed8b76095008a89","number":280,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"C82: improved upper bound 0.2519889614* (degree-104 denominators)","user":{"login":"vidigoat","id":219086731,"node_id":"U_kgDODQ7_iw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219086731?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vidigoat","html_url":"https://github.com/vidigoat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vidigoat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vidigoat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vidigoat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vidigoat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vidigoat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vidigoat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vidigoat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vidigoat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vidigoat/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Updated 9 Nov: C82 < 0.2519889614\\*.** This is 3.38·10⁻⁶ below the 5 Nov candidate 0.2519923410\\* of #330, which was built on this PR's v3 and v4. It is 1.90·10⁻⁵ below v4; the v3 and v4 rows are kept.\n\n**What is in it.**\n- Eight monic degree-104 denominators:\n  - D11_5_0 (v3), D11_12_0 and D31_5_0 (v4);\n  - one new, D51_16_0;\n  - four from #330's certificate (credited in the row).\n- 25 numerators: Doche's five P-factors, and 20 from our LLL numerator search, 14 of them new.\n\nThe search continued the CVP denominator search and LLL numerator search of v3 on one warm joint LP, over the union of our library and #330's factors.\n\n**Verification.** The same Arb checker as v2–v4 (192 bits) gives:\n- a Mahler part of [0.2519878666177742 ± 4.7·10⁻²⁶];\n- an integral upper bound of 1.095·10⁻⁶, at tolerance 10⁻¹¹;\n- in total, **B ≤ 0.25198896138704**.\n\nH1 to H3 are checked exactly. Certificate: [c82/v5](https://github.com/vidigoat/optimization-records/tree/191064e7ccd88718853fe239dfd3890a8dc0fa37/tao/certificates/c82/v5), sha256 `8a5f363c29f02fca71e99dcedfdae0bd8969cd02bbed560484d1da726175a909`.\n\n---\n\n**Updated 5 Nov (evening): C82 < 0.2520079724\\***. This is 9.95·10⁻⁶ below the 5 Nov candidate 0.2520179248\\* of #330, which was built on this PR's v3, and 5.12·10⁻⁵ below v3 (0.2520591386\\*, row kept).\n\n**What is new.**\n- Five monic degree-104 denominators: D11_5_0 from v3, and four new ones (D11_9_0, D11_12_0, D11_12_1, D31_5_0). They were found by continuing v3's CVP-enumeration denominator search, alternated with the LLL numerator search on one warm joint LP.\n- 27 numerators: Doche's P1–P4 and P6, MS360 of #301, and 21 of ours.\n- No factor of #330's 5 Nov update is used.\n\n**Verification.** The same checker as v3 (Arb, 192 bits) gives:\n- a Mahler part of [0.2520059412697726 ± 1.6·10⁻²⁶];\n- an integral upper bound of 2.031·10⁻⁶, at quadrature tolerance 10⁻¹¹;\n- in total, **B ≤ 0.25200797232846**.\n\nH1 to H3 are checked exactly.\n\nCertificate: [c82/v4](https://github.com/vidigoat/optimization-records/tree/79ce0dfb211a67ff7e387b58b0d19ff1d6accfba/tao/certificates/c82/v4), sha256 `c1981f1c4f5e1813f625c54ce952e9b5fa210f2cccbd5ac832d2a41f12ccc72f`.\n\n---\n\n**Earlier update (v3):**\n\n**C82 < 0.2520591386\\***, 3.46·10⁻⁴ below #330 (R. Pinho, 0.252404806\\*). Our checker gives the rigorous upper bound B ≤ 0.25205913852601. Arhan Canli's independent replay (comment below) encloses B ∈ [0.2520591385259547, 0.2520591385259548].\n\nThis pull request now records three of our certificates as separate rows, all in Doche's limit-point construction and R. Pinho's certificate format. All earlier rows and credits are kept.\n\n| row | bound | what is new |\n|---|---|---|\n| [Pat26] | 0.2534350402\\* | 17 new numerators from the iterated dual-weighted LLL search |\n| [Pat26b] | 0.2524177045\\* | 4 new degree-104 denominators from the CVP-enumeration search |\n| **[Pat26c]** | **0.2520591386\\*** | **3 new degree-104 denominators with normalised log M(R∘T)/208 ≈ 0.251994, 0.252086, 0.252106, below every earlier denominator** |\n\n**The new certificate:**\n- 3 monic degree-104 denominators, D = 999,999,999,960.\n- 21 numerators, deg A/D = 0.9053:\n  - Doche's P1, P2, P3, P4, P6;\n  - Pinho's MS360 (#301);\n  - two earlier library factors;\n  - 13 numerators from our LLL search.\n- Mahler part 0.25203940065826; integral part ≤ 1.974·10⁻⁵.\n\n**How it was found.** We continued our CVP denominator search of [Pat26b]. The starting library was our previous search state plus the six denominators of #330, credited there; none of them is in the final certificate. After two rounds adding single factors, the search reached factors with log M/deg ≈ 0.2521, and each later round lowered the LP by 5·10⁻⁵ to 1·10⁻⁴. The certificate is a fine-grid re-solve of the round-6 state, with exact integer multiplicities and dyadic exponents rounded down. The search was still improving.\n\n**Verification.** `checkers/vcheck.py`, the same checker as [Pat26b] and unchanged, gives B ≤ 0.25205913852601. Its printed ball radius covers Arb's arithmetic only; the integral part is an upper bound at quadrature tolerance 10⁻¹¹, so the value is an upper bound, not a two-sided enclosure. It checks:\n- H1: integer coefficients, monic denominators, positive integer multiplicities, q ≥ 0;\n- H2: deg A < D;\n- H3: exact FLINT gcds for every active pair;\n- Arb root enclosures with multiplicities summing to the degree;\n- an integral upper bound on an exact dyadic tiling (405k panels).\n\nThe float value on 2²⁰ points is 0.2520591385373. Certificate sha256 `00125f6984ad2646a79d8782ee38f5161bd24c17d4899e4af74ff3e529ba1dbe`.\n\nCertificate, checker and receipt: [vidigoat/optimization-records@197962c, tao/certificates/c82/v3](https://github.com/vidigoat/optimization-records/tree/197962c9610f583e9bc56efe37bfb994c1eeb834/tao/certificates/c82/v3).\n\n```\npython checkers/vcheck.py certificate.json --tol 1e-11 --prec 192 --target 0.2520591386\n```\n\n`scripts/check_pages.py`: 0 errors, 0 warnings. The branch is rebased on current main. If #301 or #330 merge first, their rows stay, and the README cell should show the smallest value.\n\nCredit:\n- Doche: the construction and the P-factors.\n- R. Pinho: the certificate format, the joint LP, the residue-class denominator search, the #229/#301 libraries, and the #330 factors in the starting library.\n- Grinsztajn and Épi/BakeLab: earlier factors.\n- Arhan Canli: independent replays of [Pat26], [Pat26b] and #301.\n\nFound and prepared with Claude (Anthropic) agents under V. Patankar's direction; the values are recomputed by the linked checker. They have not been verified line by line by a human expert.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-27T02:27:26Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T03:24:50Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"cee55adf1f604208ba1977f020a99